 "Mild ataxic gait but nonfocal neurological exam"], "excluded_candidates": ["Infectious aetiology (e.g., tuberculosis, CMV): constitutional symptoms may overlap but blasts are more specific for hematologic malignancy", "Metastatic visceral mass: constitutional symptoms and weight loss are concerning, but hematologic findings suggest primary marrow pathology", "Diabetic ketoacidosis or neuroglycopenia: ruled out by normal glucose and prior close endocrinology follow-up"], "alarm_features": ["Weight loss", "Night sweats", "Fever"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.6923076923076924, "posterior": 0.5347024846428898, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["35% blasts in peripheral blood is diagnostic of hematologic malignancy rather than reactive processes. No reactive condition explains such high blast percentage without marked morphologic differentiation.", "The lack of prior MPN history makes CML blast crisis less likely, but not impossible, as blast transformation can occur without a documented chronic phase. This provides weak evidence against CML/MPN as the dominant explanation."], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Is there a history of chronic myeloproliferative neoplasm (e.g., CML)?", "Are there symptoms of infection or inflammation?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Peripheral blood smear for myeloperoxidase", "Bone marrow biopsy", "Karyotype/Fluorescent in situ hybridization (FISH) for BCR-ABL"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.9, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism"}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior