sion over several days is atypical for CML blast crisis (typically acute transformation from established chronic phase) and more characteristic of de novo AML as a monophasic aggressive process.", "No findings directly contradict a de novo diagnosis of AML. The 35% blasts and subacute constitutional symptoms remain consistent with AML, though further testing is needed to confirm lineage and rule out other blast-related conditions."], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Does the patient have a documented history of chronic myeloid proliferation or prior myelodysplastic syndrome?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Bone marrow aspiration and biopsy to assess for blasts >20% and rule out lineage restriction", "Cytogenetic analysis for known AML-associated chromosomal abnormalities"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.95, "interrupt_relevance": 0.85, "level_role": "disease_class", "classification_axis": "etiology"}, "B1.2": {"id": "B1.2", "label": "Chronic Myeloid Proliferation with Blast Transformation (CML Blast Crisis / MPN Evolution)", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.1384615384615385, "posterior": 0.03713211698908958, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Subacute progression over several days is atypical for CML blast crisis (typically acute transformation from established chronic phase) and more characteristic of de novo AML as a monophasic aggressive process.", "No findings directly contradict a de novo diagnosis of AML. The 35% blasts and subacute constitutional symptoms remain consistent with AML, though further testing is needed to confirm lineage and rule out other blast-related conditions."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Are there